Condition : 9 - Demolition Management Plan  

Prior to the commencement of the development, including any demolition works and site preparation, a Demolition Management Plan shall be submitted to, and approved in writing by, the local planning authority. The approved Plan shall be adhered to throughout the demolition period. The Plan shall include:  
�	Site plan showing the position of the various elements required to support the demolition (welfare facilities, site hut/office);  
�	Confirmation that a pre-start record of site conditions on the adjoining public highway will be undertaken with Hounslow Highways and a commitment to repair any damage caused; 
�	Details of the parking for site operatives and visitors (to be indicated on the site plan); 
�	Loading and storage areas for the excavated materials; 
�	Proposed washing facilities at the site exit and a commitment to sweep adjacent roads when required and at the request of the council; 
�	Measures to ensure the safety of all users of the public highway especially cyclists and pedestrians in the vicinity of the site and especially at the access; Commitment to avoid attendance to the site by large vehicles (HGV) associated with the proposed works.   

Reason. To ensure highway safety is maintained and preserved and in the interests of air quality and neighbour amenity in accordance with policies EQ2, EQ4 and EC2 of the Local Plan (2015), coupled with the requirements of the NPPF (2023).

Condition : 13 - Ecological Management Plan  

Prior to the commencement of the development, including any demolition works, an Ecological Management Plan (EMP) shall be submitted to and approved in writing by the Local Planning Authority. The EMP shall incorporate:  
i.	details of measures to protect breeding birds, nests and eggs from mortality/damage, injury and disturbance, including avoidance by timing and/or appropriate supervision;  
ii.	details of the ecological clerk of works supervision to be put in place to monitor the clearance of vegetation to ensure no impact on undiscovered or other unexpected faunal encounters;  
iii.	details of the removal, long-term management or eradication of the invasive species found on the site,  
iv.	details of ecological enhancement, biodiversity net gains and an urban greening factor, including how a minimum urban greening factor of 0.17 and a 200% biodiversity net gain are to be delivered and achieved on site;  
v.	details of how the enhancement measures will be monitored, managed and maintained, including the long- term design objectives, management responsibilities and maintenance schedules;  
vi.	details on location and type (including specifications) of bird boxes and other ecological enhancements, maintenance and a commitment that any data collected is to be shared with the Council; including 20 x house martin nest boxes; 10 x starling nest boxes; 10 x sparrow terrace nest boxes; 10 x insect blocks; to be installed within the approved development; and  
vii.	species surveys within and around the site to demonstrate ecological enhancements.  

The development shall then be carried out in strict accordance with the approved details.  

Reason: In the interest of maintaining ecology and to result in a net gain in biodiversity in accordance with policies GB4 and GB7 of the Local Plan (2015) and policies G5, G6 and G7 of the London Plan (2021) coupled with the requirements of the NPPF (2023) and under the Wildlife and Countrys

Condition : 20 - Construction Environment Management Plan

Prior to the commencement of the development, including any demolition works and site preparation, a detailed Construction Environment Management Plan (CEMP) shall be submitted to and approved in writing by the Local Planning Authority. The CEMP shall provide details of how demolition and construction works are to be undertaken and include:
i.	The identification of stages of works;
ii.	measures to mitigate noise, dust and air quality;
iii.	details of working hours, which unless otherwise agreed with the Local Planning Authority shall be limited to 08:00 to 18:00 Monday to Friday and 08:00 to 13:00 on Saturdays);
iv.	Procedures for maintaining good public relations including complaint management, public consultation and liaison;
v.	Mitigation measured as defined in BS 5228: Parts 1 and 2: 2009 Noise and Vibration Control on Construction and Open Sites shall be used to minimise noise disturbance from construction works;
vi.	Measures to control emissions during the construction phase in line with the requirements of the Mayor's Control of Dust and Emissions during Construction and Demolition SPG.
The approved CEMP shall be adhered to throughout the construction period of the development.

Reason: In order to safeguard the amenities of adjoining residents and the amenities of the locality in accordance with Local Plan (2015) policies CC1, CC2, GB7, EQ4 and EQ5, London Plan (2021) policies D14, G6 and SI1, coupled with the requirements of the NPPF (2023).

Condition : 27 - Parking management plan

Notwithstanding the submitted details, before the development hereby permitted is first occupied or brought into use, an updated Parking Management Plan shall be submitted to and approved in writing by the Local Planning Authority. The Plan shall include the following:

(i) A commitment to review and fully justify the number of parking spaces once the end-user is known, and details of how this will be operated and enforced;
(ii) details of measures proposed to restrict parking to designated bays only and prohibit parking on the access road;
(iii) a commitment to convert passive EV bays to active and to provide additional Blue Badge bays when demand requires;
(iv) details of the operation of any gates or barriers;
(v) details of how parking will be monitored and managed during shift changeovers;
(vi) measures to ensure that all prospective occupiers are informed of the Parking Management Plan.

The parking areas and access road(s) shall thereafter be managed in compliance with the approved Parking Management Plan, unless the prior written approval of the local planning authority is obtained to secure any variation.

Reason: To ensure the scheme does not give rise to highway safety concerns and accords with the aims and objectives of the Council's sustainable transport agenda in accordance with Local Plan (2015) policy EC2 and London Plan (2021) policy T4, coupled with the requirements of the NPPF (2023).
